# Git: one PR branch

This repo uses **two long-lived git lines**:

| Branch | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `main` | Released / stable; do not commit feature work here |
| `pr/backlog-ci-dataset` | **All** feature work, agents, and open-PR commits |

## Mandatory for agents

1. **Before any commit**, confirm branch:
   ```bash
   git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD
   ```
   Must be `pr/backlog-ci-dataset`. If on `main` or any other name (`refactor/*`, `feature/*`, etc.), fix first:
   ```bash
   git fetch origin
   git checkout pr/backlog-ci-dataset
   git pull --ff-only origin pr/backlog-ci-dataset
   ```
   If `pull --ff-only` fails, stop and ask the user — do not create a new branch.

2. **Never** create or commit to ad-hoc branches (`refactor/dry-5agent`, `squash-tmp`, `backup/*`) unless the user explicitly requests a throwaway experiment branch.

3. **Push** (when asked) only to:
   ```bash
   git push origin pr/backlog-ci-dataset
   ```

4. Sync with remote before starting large work:
   ```bash
   git fetch origin
   git diff origin/main...HEAD   # scope check vs main
   ```

## Do not

- Reset `pr/backlog-ci-dataset` to a different history without user approval.
- Force-push `main`.
- Assume local `pr/backlog-ci-dataset` matches `origin/pr/backlog-ci-dataset` without `git fetch`.

Remote tracking: `origin/pr/backlog-ci-dataset` is the PR source of truth on GitHub.
